The Attorney General of India must be qualified to be a Supreme Court judge. Consider the following statements – a citizen of India so qualifies if he has been:
1. a judge of a High Court for at least 7 years;
2. an advocate of a High Court for at least 10 years;
3. a distinguished jurist in the opinion of the Chief Justice of India.
Which of the statements given above is/are correct?
